      "Students will be able to describe the properties of each state regarding shape and volume.",
      "Students will develop observation skills by classifying everyday objects based on their state.",
      "Students will understand that matter exists everywhere, including invisible forms like air."
    ],
    "key_points": [
      "Solids have a definite shape and a definite volume.",
      "Liquids have a definite volume but take the shape of their container.",
      "Gases have neither a definite shape nor a definite volume; they expand to fill their container."
    ],
    "difficulties": [
      "Understanding that gases occupy space and have mass despite being invisible.",
      "Differentiating between microscopic particle behavior (movement/spacing) and macroscopic observations.",
      "Recognizing that some materials can change states (e.g., melting ice) without changing identity."
    ],
