      "type": "Interactive Game",
      "duration": "20 minutes",
      "steps": [
        "Divide the class into groups of 5-6 representing households on a dark street.",
        "Explain that a streetlight costs $100 total. Each household values the light at $30.",
        "Ask each student to privately decide whether to contribute $20 towards the light.",
        "If total contributions reach $100, the light turns on for everyone. If not, no one gets the light.",
        "Reveal results. Discuss why many chose not to contribute despite valuing the light more than the cost (Free-Rider Problem).",
        "Discuss how mandatory taxation solves this issue."
      ],
      "learning_outcome": "Experiential understanding of the free-rider problem and collective action dilemma."
    },
    {
      "activity_name": "Good Classification Matrix",
      "type": "Group Work",
      "duration": "25 minutes",
      "steps": [
