    "teaching_objectives": [
      "Students will be able to define 'historiography' and explain its significance in understanding historical narratives.",
      "Students will distinguish between primary and secondary sources and identify their respective strengths and limitations.",
      "Students will apply source criticism techniques (origin, purpose, value, limitation) to analyze primary documents.",
      "Students will recognize how historical interpretations evolve over time due to new evidence or changing perspectives."
    ],
    "key_points": [
      "Definition of Historiography: The study of how history is written and how interpretations change.",
      "Primary vs. Secondary Sources: Direct evidence from the time period vs. analysis created later.",
      "Source Analysis Framework: OPVL (Origin, Purpose, Value, Limitation).",
      "Bias and Perspective: Understanding that all sources reflect the viewpoint of their creator.",
      "Contextualization: Placing sources within the broader social, political, and economic context of the era."
