      "Identifying Implicit Bias: Recognizing subtle biases in seemingly objective documents requires critical thinking skills.",
      "Synthesis: Connecting specific primary source details to broader historiographical debates can be challenging.",
      "Temporal Distance: Understanding the mindset of people in the past without imposing modern values (presentism)."
    ],
    "classroom_activity_design": {
      "activity_name": "The Evolving Narrative: Case Study of the Cuban Missile Crisis",
      "description": "A comparative analysis activity where students examine primary sources from 1962 and secondary historiographical analyses from different decades to see how the narrative changed.",
      "steps": [
        {
          "step_number": 1,
          "action": "Introduction (15 mins)",
          "details": "Teacher defines Historiography and Primary Sources. Brief lecture on the Cuban Missile Crisis timeline."
        },
        {
          "step_number": 2,
          "action": "Group Work - Primary Source Analysis (30 mins)",
          "details": "Divide class into groups. Group A analyzes a US ExComm meeting transcript (Oct 1962). Group B analyzes a Soviet diplomatic cable (Oct 1962). Groups complete an OPVL worksheet."
        },
        {
          "step_number": 3,
          "action": "Group Work - Historiographical Comparison (30 mins)",
          "details": "Provide excerpts from two books: one published in 1969 (Traditionalist view) and one published in 2000 (Post-Cold War view using declassified docs). Groups discuss how the interpretation differs based on available evidence."
        },
        {
          "step_number": 4,
          "action": "Class Discussion & Synthesis (15 mins)",
          "details": "Groups present findings. Teacher facilitates discussion on why interpretations changed (e.g., access to archives, end of Cold War tensions)."
        }
      ],
      "materials_needed": [
        "Transcripts of ExComm meetings (declassified)",
        "Soviet diplomatic correspondence translations",
        "Excerpts from 'The Kennedy Tapes' (1969 era text)",
        "Excerpts from 'One Hell of a Gamble' (1997/2000 era text)",
        "OPVL Worksheet templates"
      ]
    },
    "assessment_methods": [
      "Formative: Observation of group discussions and completion of OPVL worksheets.",
      "Summative: Short essay prompt asking students to compare two historians' interpretations of the same event and cite primary evidence that supports or refutes each view."
    ],
    "resources_and_references": [
      "National Archives Education Resources",
      "Stanford History Education Group (SHEG) Lesson Plans",
