      "Build intuition for limits and derivatives without heavy abstraction."
    ],
    "content_description": "This task focuses on mastering algebraic functions by visualizing them in real-world contexts. Instead of starting with abstract equations, you will analyze motion data to understand how changes in one variable affect another, laying the groundwork for calculus concepts like derivatives.",
    "activity_steps": [
      {
        "step_number": 1,
        "title": "Visual Warm-Up",
        "instruction": "Open a graphing tool (like Desmos or GeoGebra). Plot three different linear functions (y = mx + b) with varying slopes. Observe how changing 'm' visually steepens or flattens the line.",
