      },
      {
        "step_number": 2,
        "title": "Practical Application: The Road Trip",
        "instruction": "Imagine a car trip where distance is plotted against time. You have data points: (0 hours, 0 miles), (1 hour, 60 miles), (2 hours, 120 miles). Plot these points and draw the line connecting them.",
        "visual_focus": "See the straight line represent constant speed."
      },
      {
        "step_number": 3,
        "title": "Complex Problem-Solving Scaffold",
        "instruction": "Now, introduce a curve. Data points: (0, 0), (1, 40), (2, 120). Plot these. Notice the line isn't straight. Calculate the average speed between hour 0-1 and hour 1-2 separately. Compare the two results.",
