      {
        "step_number": 2,
        "action": "Apply the Sum Rule",
        "detail": "According to the sum rule of differentiation, the derivative of a sum is equal to the sum of the derivatives. Therefore, f'(x) = d/dx(e^x) + d/dx(x^2)."
